# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type }})

{{ .Description }}

A pool has at most one health monitor, and this resource manages it. To move a
monitor from the removed `healthmonitor` attribute of
`gcore_cloud_load_balancer_pool`, import it into this resource. See the
migration steps in the `gcore_cloud_load_balancer_pool` documentation.

Changing `type` replaces the monitor. The pool has no health check between
the delete and the create.

## Example Usage

### HTTP health monitor

Probes `/health` with GET and treats 200 or 204 as healthy.

{{tffile "examples/resources/gcore_cloud_load_balancer_pool_health_monitor/http-monitor.tf"}}

### TCP health monitor

Checks that members accept a TCP connection on their `protocol_port`, or on
`monitor_port` if the member sets one.

{{tffile "examples/resources/gcore_cloud_load_balancer_pool_health_monitor/tcp-monitor.tf"}}

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

